<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="A sanitized home-server infrastructure case study."><title>Monitoring · Home Server</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"></head><body><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="../index.html" aria-label="Engineering Notebook home"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4h6v6H4zM14 4h6v6h-6zM4 14h6v6H4zM14 14h6v6h-6z"/></svg><span class="nav-label">Engineering Notebook</span></a><nav aria-label="Home-server navigation"><div class="home-server-links"><a href="/home-server/">Overview</a><a href="/home-server/hardware/">Hardware</a><a href="/home-server/security/">Security</a><a class="active" href="/home-server/monitoring/">Monitoring</a><a href="/home-server/backups/">Backups</a><a href="/home-server/services/">Services</a><a href="/home-server/lessons/">Lessons</a></div><a href="/projects/"><span class="nav-label">← Projects</span></a></nav></header><main><section class="intro section-shell"><p class="eyebrow">HOME SERVER / MONITORING</p><h1>Monitoring</h1><p class="lede">Once the server was running, it needed to tell me when it was unhappy before I started blaming the wrong cable.</p><button class="intro-scroll-cue" type="button" aria-label="Scroll to next section"></button></section><section class="section-shell"><div class="feature-card"><div class="card-kicker">OBSERVABILITY</div><h3>Dashboards turned “it feels slow” into evidence.</h3><p>Docker Compose runs Grafana, Prometheus, Node Exporter, and a NUT exporter. Prometheus scrapes the Flashpoint application, host metrics, and UPS metrics. Grafana turns those measurements into dashboards for CPU, memory, disk, network traffic, UPS battery, runtime, power draw, and application behavior.</p><p>Discord notifications cover UPS battery operation, missing server metrics, and low root-disk space. The alerts are useful because they describe a condition that needs action, not because they make the dashboard look busier.</p></div></section><section class="section-shell"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">VERIFIED BEHAVIOR</p><h2>Monitoring was tested as a system.</h2></div><div class="note-grid"><article class="note-card"><span>01</span><h3>Power loss</h3><p>NUT detected battery operation, waited through the configured timer, and shut the server down safely.</p></article><article class="note-card"><span>02</span><h3>Recovery</h3><p>After reboot, Docker, NUT, Tailscale, Grafana, Prometheus, and the application returned successfully.</p></article><article class="note-card"><span>03</span><h3>Application</h3><p>Flashpoint appeared in Prometheus and Grafana with service health, request rate, outcomes, inventory, and latency.</p></article></div></section></main><script is:inline src="../../scroll-cue.js"></script></body></html>